 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Textured Gaussians](8061-textured-gaussians.md)
-Textured Gaussians replace the standard spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients used for view-dependent color in 3D Gaussian Splatting with explicit 2D textures mapped onto each primitive. This method solves the limitation of SH representations in capturing high-frequency appearance details without requiring an increase in the number of primitives. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like View-Dependent Appearance Representations by utilizing spatial UV sampling rather than directional basis functions, enabling high-fidelity texture reconstruction. See [Textured Gaussians](8061-textured-gaussians.md).
